            <ArticleTitle>[The CASS-CHOU study of mesenteric angina. The comparative effects of cassoulet and sauerkraut with sausages].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>689-92</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The goal of study was evaluate in 1,837 consecutive patients the comparative effects of French cassoulet (CASS) and international sauerkraut (CHOU). After procedures of exclusion classical, 8 patients could be evaluated and received in a randomised, doubleblind, crossover protocol an mouth dose of 22.5 g/kg of CASS or CHOU. The results show a very significative difference between the 2 products. A regular absorption of couscous is therefore recommended.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
